-- title:
--   Eichler–Shimura: Galois representations from Hecke characters on VₚJ₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and a prime $p$, a discrete valuation domain $O$ with fraction field $K$, a ring homomorphism $i_0\colon\mathbb Z_p\to O$, and assume $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O$. Let $J_0(N)$ denote [`ModularCurve.JZero N`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L115), the degree-zero divisor class group of the modular function field of level $N$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, equipped with the Hecke-algebra action [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleBar N`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L82), and let $\mathcal A=$ `rationalHeckeAlgebra` be the $\mathbb Q_p$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb Q_p}(V_pJ_0(N))$ generated by the image of the Hecke algebra under `rationalHeckeRep`. The assertion is: for every ring homomorphism $\Lambda\colon\mathcal A\to K$ with $\Lambda(c\cdot 1)=i_0(c)$ in $K$ for all $c\in\mathbb Z_p$, there is a [`GaloisRepAdic O`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16), that is a finite free $O$-module $V$ with $\operatorname{rank}_OV=2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ to $\operatorname{End}_O(V)$ which is adically continuous (for each $n$ some finite subextension $L/\mathbb Q$ has $\rho(\sigma)v-v\in\mathfrak m_O^n V$ for all $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise and all $v$), such that: (i) for every prime $\ell\nmid Np$, every $a\in O$ whose image in $K$ equals $\Lambda$ of the class of `heckeGen ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩` (the polynomial generator $T_\ell$), every valuation subring $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $A$ acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x\mapsto x^\ell$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-aX+\ell$; and (ii) for every prime $\ell\nmid Np$, every valuation subring over $\ell$ and every $\sigma$ in the image of its inertia subgroup, $\rho(\sigma)=1$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura construction in coefficient-agnostic form: a character of the $p$-adic Hecke algebra acting on the rational Tate module of $J_0(N)$, with values in the fraction field of a discrete valuation ring, is converted into a rank-two adically continuous Galois representation over that ring with the expected Frobenius characteristic polynomials and unramifiedness away from $Np$. It is used by [`CuspForm.exists_galoisRep_of_point`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_galoisRep_of_point) and by [`ModularCurve.exists_matrixRep_trace_det_frobenius_of_heckeTorsion_ne_bot`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_matrixRep_trace_det_frobenius_of_heckeTorsion_ne_bot), and thereby supplies the Galois representation attached to a normalised eigenform.
